 - **Partner self-serve signup ends the admin-activation prerequisite.** A partner can subscribe end-to-end without an admin pre-creating their venue: the full-screen wizard at `/owner/signup` collects name → email → password → address → geofence → review, creates a hidden `venues` row + owner account, and hands off to Stripe Checkout; the webhook unhides the venue on first paid activation. Flag-gated behind `NEXT_PUBLIC_SELF_SERVE_SIGNUP_ENABLED` (`isSelfServeSignupEnabled()` in `lib/selfServeSignup.ts`) — off = `/owner/register`'s venue-lookup flow, fully inert; on = `/owner/register` redirects to `/owner/signup` and the `/info` partner CTAs point there. **Admin Activate-a-Venue (`components/admin/mobile/ActivateVenueFlow.tsx`) survives** for ops: offline-billed venues, a second venue for an existing owner (self-serve is one venue per email), and support fixes. Plan + as-built: `docs/partner-self-serve-signup-plan.md`; ops cutover + the `GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY` referrer restriction: `docs/self-serve-signup-runbook.md`. **Status (2026-09-08):** built, `/code-review`'d, and all 15 findings fixed across `docs/self-serve-signup-review-fixes-plan.md` Phases 1–7 (claim-path privilege escalation, atomic Postgres rate limiter, fail-closed public Maps key, reveal reconciler, and the "delete the second copy" cleanups). The flag is **not yet flipped** — what gates it is Phase 8's ops sequence: set `GOOGLE_MAPS_BROWSER_KEY`, re-verify admin + player Maps, re-run `/code-review`, redeploy, then close the device checklist.
